{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Esey7yq1su8Bn124fAnbt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Claim 1 弱化为 ''convergence on retrieval-heavy tasks with suggestive\n2\t  evidence on related benchmarks''。 LAMBADA 仍为唯一 BH-FDR 显著锚点，但 exp-011 新 benchmark\n3\t  方向一致性 + GDN-excluded ARC-Easy 改善 构成 converging evidence pattern。exp-004 以描述性证据呈现，避免\n4\t  mechanistic language。 exp-005 未扩展架构数量。exp-007 部分解释 340M rebound 但留有未解问题。 Claim 3\n5\t  per-example divergence 成为论文相对最强的独立贡献。目标 EMNLP Findings，honest framing。\n6\t\n7\t  '\n8\timagined_experiments:\n9\t- name: Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\n10\t  plan_id: exp-001\n11\t  description: 计算 6 个 benchmark 在每个 attention ratio 下的 cross-architecture std，建立 task\n12\t    taxonomy\n13\t  expected_results:\n14\t    LAMBADA_rho: -1.0\n15\t    LAMBADA_p: 0.008\n16\t    LAMBADA_taxonomy: retrieval-dependent\n17\t    LAMBADA_std_reduction_pct: 79\n18\t    HellaSwag_rho: 0.3\n19\t    HellaSwag_p: 0.742\n20\t    HellaSwag_taxonomy: reasoning-dependent\n21\t    ARC_Challenge_rho: 0.6\n22\t    ARC_Challenge_p: 0.883\n23\t    ARC_Challenge_taxonomy: reasoning-dependent\n24\t    Winogrande_rho: 0.1\n25\t    Winogrande_p: 0.608\n26\t    Winogrande_taxonomy: reasoning-dependent\n27\t    ARC_Easy_rho: -0.7\n28\t    ARC_Easy_p: 0.117\n29\t    ARC_Easy_taxonomy: mixed\n30\t    MMLU_rho: -0.7\n31\t    MMLU_p: 0.117\n32\t    MMLU_taxonomy: mixed\n33\t    significant_count: 1/6\n34\t  result_rationale: '已完成实验。LAMBADA 作为 last-word-in-context retrieval task，attention\n35\t    直接增强了从上文提取目标词的能力， 且三种架构的 baseline 缺陷高度同质（都缺少 global attention），因此 attention 的补偿效应方向一致、\n36\t    幅度相近，产生强 convergence。Reasoning tasks (HellaSwag, ARC-C, Winogrande) 依赖多步推理链， attention\n37\t    的增益是架构特异性的（不同 recurrent backbone 的 bottleneck 不同），所以不 converge。 ARC-Easy 和 MMLU\n38\t    介于两者之间：含部分 retrieval 成分但也需要 world knowledge，产生 suggestive 但不显著的趋势。\n39\t\n40\t    '\n41\t  tables:\n42\t  - name: 'Table 1: Task-specificity of convergence effect'\n43\t    columns:\n44\t    - Benchmark\n45\t    - Task Type\n46\t    - ρ (Spearman)\n47\t    - p (exact perm.)\n48\t    - Std Reduction %\n49\t    - Taxonomy\n50\t    rows:\n51\t    - - LAMBADA\n52\t      - last-word retrieval\n53\t      - -1.0\n54\t      - 0.008\n55\t      - 79%\n56\t      - retrieval-dependent\n57\t    - - ARC-Easy\n58\t      - factual QA\n59\t      - -0.7\n60\t      - 0.117\n61\t      - 42%\n62\t      - mixed\n63\t    - - MMLU\n64\t      - knowledge QA\n65\t      - -0.7\n66\t      - 0.117\n67\t      - 38%\n68\t      - mixed\n69\t    - - HellaSwag\n70\t      - commonsense reasoning\n71\t      - 0.3\n72\t      - 0.742\n73\t      - +15%\n74\t      - reasoning-dependent\n75\t    - - Winogrande\n76\t      - coreference reasoning\n77\t      - 0.1\n78\t      - 0.608\n79\t      - +8%\n80\t      - reasoning-dependent\n81\t    - - ARC-Challenge\n82\t      - multi-step reasoning\n83\t      - 0.6\n84\t      - 0.883\n85\t      - +22%\n86\t      - reasoning-dependent\n87\t  figures_description:\n88\t  - 'Fig 1: 6-panel grid, 每个 benchmark 一个 panel。X 轴 = attention ratio (h0→h24), Y\n89\t    轴 = cross-arch std。LAMBADA panel 展示清晰下降趋势，reasoning tasks 平坦或上升。'\n90\t  analysis: 'Taxonomy 清晰分为三档：retrieval-dependent (LAMBADA, 强 convergence)、mixed (ARC-Easy/MMLU,\n91\t    suggestive)、 reasoning-dependent (HellaSwag/Winogrande/ARC-C, 无 convergence 或反向)。这支持\n92\t    attention 的 equalizer 效应是 task-modulated 的解释——当 task 的关键 bottleneck 恰好是 global\n93\t    context retrieval 时， attention 对所有架构提供相似的补偿。\n94\t\n95\t    '\n96\t- name: Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\n97\t  plan_id: exp-002\n98\t  description: 对 HellaSwag/ARC-Easy/ARC-Challenge 收集 --log_samples per-example 数据，验证\n99\t    task-specificity 在 per-example 层面的表现\n100\t  expected_results:\n101\t    n_models_rerun: 13\n102\t    models_340m:\n103\t    - RetNet×5\n104\t    - HGRN2×5\n105\t    models_1_3b:\n106\t    - GDN h3-1\n107\t    - GDN h6-1\n108\t    - GDN h24-1\n109\t    HellaSwag_per_example_n: 10042\n110\t    ARC_Easy_per_example_n: 2376\n111\t    ARC_Challenge_per_example_n: 1172\n112\t    HellaSwag_cross_arch_jaccard_helped: 0.18\n113\t    HellaSwag_cross_arch_jaccard_hurt: 0.15\n114\t    ARC_Easy_cross_arch_jaccard_helped: 0.14\n115\t    ARC_Easy_cross_arch_jaccard_hurt: 0.11\n116\t    ARC_Challenge_cross_arch_jaccard_helped: 0.12\n117\t    ARC_Challenge_cross_arch_jaccard_hurt: 0.1\n118\t    LAMBADA_reference_jaccard: 0.08\n119\t    task_specificity_per_example_confirmed: true\n120\t    reasoning_task_pattern: systematic_but_architecture_specific\n121\t    gpu_hours_actual: 18\n122\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下，per-example 数据成功收集但揭示了 nuanced pattern：reasoning tasks\n123\t    的 per-example Jaccard 比 LAMBADA 高（0.10-0.18 vs 0.05-0.10），说明 attention 在 reasoning\n124\t    tasks 上影响的样本集有更多重叠， 但这种重叠并不 translate 为 aggregate convergence（因为影响方向和幅度是架构特异的）。\n125\t    LAMBADA 的低 Jaccard 反而说明：aggregate convergence 不是因为 attention 帮助了相同的样本， 而是因为不同样本的帮助在\n126\t    aggregate 层面恰好相互补偿到相似水平。 这加强了 Claim 3 的 underspecification 叙事——convergence 和 per-example\n127\t    agreement 是正交的维度。 Reasoning tasks 展示 \"systematic but architecture-specific\" pattern：每个架构内\n128\t    helped/hurt 有结构性， 但跨架构差异大到无法 aggregate converge。\n129\t\n130\t    '\n131\t  tables:\n132\t  - name: 'Table: Per-example overlap (Jaccard) across benchmarks at h3-1, 1.3B'\n133\t    columns:\n134\t    - Benchmark\n135\t    - Jaccard (helped)\n136\t    - Jaccard (hurt)\n137\t    - LAMBADA ref.\n138\t    - Interpretation\n139\t    rows:\n140\t    - - LAMBADA\n141\t      - 0.08\n142\t      - 0.07\n143\t      - —\n144\t      - Low overlap → different samples helped per arch\n145\t    - - HellaSwag\n146\t      - 0.18\n147\t      - 0.15\n148\t      - 2.3×\n149\t      - Higher overlap but no aggregate convergence\n150\t    - - ARC-Easy\n151\t      - 0.14\n152\t      - 0.11\n153\t      - 1.8×\n154\t      - Moderate overlap, suggestive convergence\n155\t    - - ARC-Challenge\n156\t      - 0.12\n157\t      - 0.1\n158\t      - 1.5×\n159\t      - Moderate overlap, no convergence\n160\t  figures_description:\n161\t  - 'Fig: Jaccard heatmap (3 arch pairs × 4 benchmarks), 颜色编码 per-example overlap。LAMBADA\n162\t    行最冷（低 overlap），HellaSwag 行最暖。'\n163\t  - 'Fig: Per-example effect scatter (baseline ppl vs Δ accuracy) for each benchmark\n164\t    × architecture，展示 reasoning tasks 的架构特异性 pattern。'\n165\t  analysis: 'Per-example 数据确认 task-specificity 不仅存在于 aggregate 层面，也存在于 per-example\n166\t    层面，但方式不同于预期。 Reasoning tasks 有更高的 per-example overlap（attention 倾向于影响某些 \"universally\n167\t    tricky\" 样本）， 但影响的方向和幅度架构特异。LAMBADA 的低 overlap + 高 aggregate convergence 构成最强的\n168\t    underspecification 案例。 exp-002 的结论：Claim 1 的 task-specificity 在 per-example 层面同样成立但机制更复杂；\n169\t    Claim 3 的 per-example divergence 在 LAMBADA 上最极端，但在所有 tasks 上都存在（程度不同）。\n170\t\n171\t    '\n172\t- name: Attention weight extraction and visualization\n173\t  plan_id: exp-004\n174\t  description: 提取 3 种架构 h3-1 配置的 attention weights，分析与 helped/hurt sample 的关联\n175\t  expected_results:\n176\t    n_models_analyzed: 3\n177\t    attention_configs: h3-1 (1 attention layer in 3-layer block)\n178\t    n_lambada_samples_analyzed: 500\n179\t    attn_entropy_GDN_mean: 3.42\n180\t    attn_entropy_RetNet_mean: 3.18\n181\t    attn_entropy_HGRN2_mean: 3.55\n182\t    attn_pattern_helped_hurt_correlation_GDN: 0.22\n183\t    attn_pattern_helped_hurt_correlation_RetNet: 0.18\n184\t    attn_pattern_helped_hurt_correlation_HGRN2: 0.25\n185\t    mean_attn_effect_correlation: 0.22\n186\t    cross_arch_attn_similarity_cosine: 0.35\n187\t    attn_focus_last_sentence_pct_GDN: 62\n188\t    attn_focus_last_sentence_pct_RetNet: 55\n189\t    attn_focus_last_sentence_pct_HGRN2: 58\n190\t    helped_vs_hurt_attn_entropy_diff_p: 0.08\n191\t    gpu_hours_actual: 3.5\n192\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下，attention-effect correlation 落在 0.15-0.30 区间（实际均值 0.22）。\n193\t    这不足以做 strong mechanistic claim，但足以做描述性报告。原因： (1) attention weights 只是 model 行为的\n194\t    partial view——per-example 效果由 attention + recurrent backbone 的交互决定，单看 attention\n195\t    只能捕获部分 variance。 (2) h3-1 配置仅 1 层 attention（在 3 层 block 中），信息密度有限。 (3) 不同架构的 attention\n196\t    确实 focus 在不同位置（cross-arch cosine similarity 仅 0.35）， 这与 per-example divergence\n197\t    一致——架构之间 attention 的 \"关注点\" 不同。 (4) 所有架构的 attention 都倾向于 focus on last sentence（55-62%），这与\n198\t    LAMBADA 的 retrieval nature 一致， 但具体 token-level focus 差异显著。 Helped 样本的 attention\n199\t    entropy 略低于 hurt 样本（p=0.08），暗示 attention 在 \"知道该看哪里\" 时更有效， 但这只是 suggestive。\n200\t\n201\t    '\n202\t  tables:\n203\t  - name: 'Table: Attention pattern statistics by architecture (h3-1, 1.3B, LAMBADA)'\n204\t    columns:\n205\t    - Architecture\n206\t    - Mean Entropy\n207\t    - Last-Sentence Focus %\n208\t    - Helped-Hurt Corr.\n209\t    - Helped Entropy\n210\t    - Hurt Entropy\n211\t    rows:\n212\t    - - GDN\n213\t      - 3.42\n214\t      - 62%\n215\t      - 0.22\n216\t      - 3.31\n217\t      - 3.52\n218\t    - - RetNet\n219\t      - 3.18\n220\t      - 55%\n221\t      - 0.18\n222\t      - 3.1\n223\t      - 3.28\n224\t    - - HGRN2\n225\t      - 3.55\n226\t      - 58%\n227\t      - 0.25\n228\t      - 3.42\n229\t      - 3.65\n230\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-architecture attention similarity'\n231\t    columns:\n232\t    - Arch Pair\n233\t    - Cosine Sim (mean attn)\n234\t    - Cosine Sim (helped subset)\n235\t    - Cosine Sim (hurt subset)\n236\t    rows:\n237\t    - - GDN–RetNet\n238\t      - 0.33\n239\t      - 0.28\n240\t      - 0.31\n241\t    - - GDN–HGRN2\n242\t      - 0.38\n243\t      - 0.35\n244\t      - 0.33\n245\t    - - RetNet–HGRN2\n246\t      - 0.34\n247\t      - 0.3\n248\t      - 0.29\n249\t  figures_description:\n250\t  - 'Fig: Attention heatmap (3 panels, one per arch) on 5 representative LAMBADA examples,\n251\t    showing divergent focus patterns across architectures on the same input.'\n252\t  - 'Fig: Scatter plot of per-sample attention entropy vs Δ accuracy for each architecture.\n253\t    Weak negative trend (r≈0.18-0.25) with wide scatter.'\n254\t  analysis: 'Attention patterns 确认三种架构的 attention 在 same input 上 focus 不同位置（cosine\n255\t    sim ≈ 0.35）， 这与 per-example Jaccard < 0.10 一致。但 attention-effect correlation 仅\n256\t    0.22，不足以说 \"attention pattern 决定了 which samples are helped\"——只能说 \"attention patterns\n257\t    differ across architectures on affected samples\"。Paper 中以描述性语言呈现：\"We observe that\n258\t    attention allocation patterns diverge across architectures (mean cosine similarity\n259\t    = 0.35), consistent with the per-example divergence reported in Section X. However,\n260\t    the modest correlation between attention statistics and per-example effects (r\n261\t    = 0.22) suggests that attention weights alone do not fully account for the architecture-specific\n262\t    patterns.\" 避免 \"mechanistic\" 一词。\n263\t\n264\t    '\n265\t- name: Architecture expansion check\n266\t  plan_id: exp-005\n267\t  description: 搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 和其他来源，寻找额外 hybrid 架构（Mamba hybrids, RWKV hybrids\n268\t    等）\n269\t  expected_results:\n270\t    additional_architectures_found: 0\n271\t    wang_et_al_architectures_checked:\n272\t    - GatedDeltaNet\n273\t    - RetNet\n274\t    - HGRN2\n275\t    - DeltaNet\n276\t    - RWKV6\n277\t    - Mamba\n278\t    hybrid_configs_available:\n279\t    - GatedDeltaNet\n280\t    - RetNet\n281\t    - HGRN2\n282\t    non_hybrid_only:\n283\t    - DeltaNet\n284\t    - RWKV6\n285\t    - Mamba\n286\t    reason_no_expansion: Wang et al. model zoo 中只有 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 有 attention-hybrid\n287\t      配置；DeltaNet/RWKV6/Mamba 仅有 pure recurrent。外部无 compatible hybrid checkpoints。\n288\t    n_architectures_final: 3\n289\t    gpu_hours_actual: 0\n290\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：exp-005 未找到可评估的额外架构。 Wang et al. 的 model zoo 设计上只为\n291\t    GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 提供了 hybrid (attention-augmented) 配置， 因为这三种是他们论文的重点对比对象。DeltaNet、RWKV6、Mamba\n292\t    等只有 pure recurrent checkpoints， 没有对应的 hybrid variants。外部开源社区（HuggingFace、GitHub）的\n293\t    hybrid checkpoints 要么训练设置不同 （不同数据、不同 tokenizer），要么规模不匹配，无法做 controlled comparison。\n294\t    因此 n=3 架构是硬限制。Paper 在 Limitations 中诚实说明：\"Our analysis is limited to three architectures\n295\t    with publicly available hybrid configurations. Extending to Mamba-2 or RWKV-6\n296\t    hybrids requires training new models, which we leave to future work.\"\n297\t\n298\t    '\n299\t  tables: []\n300\t  figures_description: []\n301\t  analysis: '未产生新数据。n=3 限制通过两种方式 mitigate： (1) 论证 3 architectures × 5 attention ratios\n302\t    × 2 scales = 30 model configurations 提供了足够的统计结构； (2) per-example analysis 提供 5153\n303\t    data points per pairwise comparison，补偿了架构数量的不足。 Reviewer Concern D 的回应策略不变。\n304\t\n305\t    '\n306\t- name: 7B model evaluation — CANCELLED\n307\t  plan_id: exp-006\n308\t  description: 7B 模型不可用，已取消。预算重新分配。\n309\t  expected_results:\n310\t    status: cancelled\n311\t    reason: Wang et al. 仅提供 340M + 1.3B (72 models total)\n312\t  result_rationale: Wang et al. model zoo 不包含 7B 规模模型。无外部可比较的 hybrid 7B checkpoints。\n313\t  tables: []\n314\t  figures_description: []\n315\t  analysis: 预算重新分配给 exp-002 和 exp-004。Claim 2 限制为 binary scale contrast。\n316\t- name: 340M rebound mechanism analysis\n317\t  plan_id: exp-007\n318\t  description: 分析 340M 在 attn=8 处的 non-monotonic rebound，与 1.3B 做 per-example 对比\n319\t  expected_results:\n320\t    rebound_attention_ratio: h8 (8/24 attention layers)\n321\t    rebound_magnitude_std_increase: 35-40% relative to h6 minimum\n322\t    n_rebound_samples_340m: 280\n323\t    n_rebound_samples_overlap_with_1_3b_hurt: 95\n324\t    overlap_pct: 34\n325\t    rebound_sample_characteristics:\n326\t      mean_context_length: 42.3\n327\t      mean_target_frequency_rank: 8500\n328\t      mean_baseline_ppl: 4.8\n329\t    partial_explanation_pct: 60\n330\t    capacity_saturation_hypothesis: supported_but_not_conclusive\n331\t    training_tokens_confound: acknowledged_not_resolved\n332\t    arch_specific_rebound:\n333\t      GDN_340m_rebound: moderate (std +30%)\n334\t      RetNet_340m_rebound: strong (std +55%)\n335\t      HGRN2_340m_rebound: weak (std +20%)\n336\t    gpu_hours_actual: 2\n337\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：340M rebound 可部分解释但非完全清晰。 部分解释（~60%）：340M 模型在 h8\n338\t    ratio 时，attention 层数已占 1/3 的 model capacity， 对于小模型来说 attention 的参数开销（QKV projections）挤占了\n339\t    recurrent backbone 的表达能力， 导致某些样本从 \"helped by attention\" 回退到 \"hurt by capacity\n340\t    reallocation\"。 具体表现为：rebound 样本与 1.3B 的 hurt 样本有 34% 重叠——这些是 \"需要 attention 但也需要\n341\t    足够 recurrent capacity 来编码上下文\" 的样本。1.3B 有足够 capacity 同时支持两者。 未解释部分（~40%）：不同架构的\n342\t    rebound 幅度差异大（RetNet 最强 +55%，HGRN2 最弱 +20%）， 暗示 rebound 不仅是 capacity issue，还与\n343\t    backbone 的 inductive bias 有关。 训练 token 数量差异（340M: 20B tokens, 1.3B: 100B tokens）作为\n344\t    confound 被承认但无法分离—— 需要 controlled training runs 才能解开，超出本文 scope。\n345\t\n346\t    '\n347\t  tables:\n348\t  - name: 'Table: 340M rebound characterization by architecture'\n349\t    columns:\n350\t    - Architecture\n351\t    - h6 Std\n352\t    - h8 Std\n353\t    - Rebound %\n354\t    - N Rebound Samples\n355\t    - Overlap with 1.3B Hurt %\n356\t    rows:\n357\t    - - GDN\n358\t      - 0.018\n359\t      - 0.023\n360\t      - +30%\n361\t      - 85\n362\t      - 38%\n363\t    - - RetNet\n364\t      - 0.015\n365\t      - 0.023\n366\t      - +55%\n367\t      - 120\n368\t      - 31%\n369\t    - - HGRN2\n370\t      - 0.02\n371\t      - 0.024\n372\t      - +20%\n373\t      - 75\n374\t      - 33%\n375\t  - name: 'Table: Rebound sample characteristics vs non-rebound'\n376\t    columns:\n377\t    - Feature\n378\t    - Rebound Samples\n379\t    - Non-Rebound\n380\t    - p (MW-U)\n381\t    rows:\n382\t    - - Context length (tokens)\n383\t      - 42.3\n384\t      - 35.1\n385\t      - 0.03\n386\t    - - Target freq rank\n387\t      - 8500\n388\t      - 6200\n389\t      - 0.07\n390\t    - - Baseline ppl (340M)\n391\t      - 4.8\n392\t      - 3.5\n393\t      - 0.01\n394\t    - - Baseline ppl (1.3B)\n395\t      - 3.1\n396\t      - 2.8\n397\t      - 0.22\n398\t  figures_description:\n399\t  - 'Fig: Cross-arch std trajectory at 340M showing non-monotonic rebound at h8, with\n400\t    1.3B monotonic curve overlaid for contrast.'\n401\t  - 'Fig: Venn diagram of rebound samples at 340M vs hurt samples at 1.3B, showing\n402\t    34% overlap.'\n403\t  analysis: 'Binary contrast narrative：1.3B 的 monotonic convergence vs 340M 的 non-monotonic\n404\t    rebound 表明 \"convergence requires sufficient capacity\"。Rebound 样本是 \"harder\" samples（higher\n405\t    baseline ppl, longer context），这些样本在 340M 下面临 capacity-attention tradeoff。 Paper\n406\t    framing：\"The non-monotonic pattern at 340M suggests a capacity threshold: smaller\n407\t    models face a tradeoff between recurrent backbone capacity and attention coverage,\n408\t    with the rebound at h8 disproportionately affecting longer-context, higher-difficulty\n409\t    examples (baseline ppl 4.8 vs 3.5, p=0.01).\" 诚实承认：training token confound 和 architecture-specific\n410\t    rebound variance 未完全解释。 这足以支持 Claim 2 的 binary contrast framing，但不足以做 extrapolation\n411\t    或 general scaling law claim。\n412\t\n413\t    '\n414\t- name: Helped/hurt sample characterization\n415\t  plan_id: exp-003\n416\t  description: 分析 LAMBADA 上每种架构的 helped/hurt 样本特征（surface features + perplexity）\n417\t  expected_results:\n418\t    phase1_surface_features:\n419\t      GDN_helped: 462\n420\t      GDN_hurt: 615\n421\t      GDN_surface_significant: false\n422\t      HGRN2_helped: 548\n423\t      HGRN2_hurt: 395\n424\t      HGRN2_surface_significant: false\n425\t      RetNet_helped: 426\n426\t      RetNet_hurt: 495\n427\t      RetNet_context_length_p: 0.012\n428\t      RetNet_context_length_r: -0.096\n429\t      RetNet_unique_tokens_p: 0.009\n430\t      RetNet_unique_tokens_r: -0.099\n431\t      cross_arch_difference_significant: false\n432\t    phase2_perplexity:\n433\t      GDN_r_rb: -0.04\n434\t      GDN_p: 0.209\n435\t      RetNet_r_rb: -0.02\n436\t      RetNet_p: 0.659\n437\t      HGRN2_r_rb: -0.04\n438\t      HGRN2_p: 0.248\n439\t      within_arch_significant: false\n440\t      cross_arch_hurt_KW_p: 0.0005\n441\t      cross_arch_helped_KW_p: 0.02\n442\t  result_rationale: '已完成实验。Within-architecture：surface features 和 baseline perplexity\n443\t    均无法区分 helped/hurt 样本（所有 within-arch p > 0.2，effect size 极小）。这 rules out trivial\n444\t    explanations—— 不是简单的 \"长句子被 attention 帮助\" 或 \"难样本被帮助\"。 Cross-architecture：不同架构 hurt\n445\t    的样本有 systematically different baseline difficulty profiles (KW p=0.0005)。这表明每种架构\n446\t    \"struggle with\" 不同难度分布的样本，attention 帮助/伤害的样本 子集因此不同。这是 structured diversity, not\n447\t    random noise——支持 Claim 3。\n448\t\n449\t    '\n450\t  tables:\n451\t  - name: 'Table: Within-architecture perplexity analysis'\n452\t    columns:\n453\t    - Architecture\n454\t    - Helped Mean PPL\n455\t    - Hurt Mean PPL\n456\t    - U statistic\n457\t    - p\n458\t    - r_rb\n459\t    rows:\n460\t    - - GDN\n461\t      - 3.37\n462\t      - 3.34\n463\t      - 148410\n464\t      - 0.209\n465\t      - -0.045\n466\t    - - RetNet\n467\t      - 3.44\n468\t      - 3.42\n469\t      - 107210\n470\t      - 0.659\n471\t      - -0.017\n472\t    - - HGRN2\n473\t      - 3.38\n474\t      - 3.35\n475\t      - 112999\n476\t      - 0.248\n477\t      - -0.044\n478\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-architecture Kruskal-Wallis tests'\n479\t    columns:\n480\t    - Sample Type\n481\t    - KW H\n482\t    - p\n483\t    - Interpretation\n484\t    rows:\n485\t    - - Hurt samples\n486\t      - —\n487\t      - 0.0005\n488\t      - Architectures hurt samples with different difficulty profiles\n489\t    - - Helped samples\n490\t      - —\n491\t      - 0.02\n492\t      - Weaker but significant cross-arch difference\n493\t  figures_description:\n494\t  - 'Fig: Violin plots of baseline perplexity distributions for hurt samples, split\n495\t    by architecture. Visually distinct distributions despite non-significant within-arch\n496\t    effects.'\n497\t  analysis: 'Two-level finding：(1) within-arch opacity (attention effects 无法用 surface\n498\t    features/perplexity 预测)， (2) cross-arch structure (不同架构的 affected samples 有 systematically\n499\t    different profiles)。 这同时加强 Claim 3 的两个方面——divergence 不是 random noise（structured），\n500\t    但也不是 trivially predictable（opaque to standard features）。\n501\t\n502\t    '\n503\t- name: Statistical robustness framework\n504\t  plan_id: exp-008\n505\t  description: Bootstrap CIs、multiple comparison correction、GDN-excluded sensitivity\n506\t    analysis\n507\t  expected_results:\n508\t    LAMBADA_rho: -1.0\n509\t    LAMBADA_exact_p_two_tailed: 0.0167\n510\t    LAMBADA_bonferroni_adj_p: 0.1\n511\t    LAMBADA_bh_fdr_adj_p: 0.1\n512\t    bootstrap_ci_lower: -1.0\n513\t    bootstrap_ci_upper: -0.7\n514\t    bootstrap_ci_crosses_zero: false\n515\t    bootstrap_n_valid: 8875\n516\t    bootstrap_n_total: 10000\n517\t    bca_degenerate: true\n518\t    gdn_excluded_LAMBADA_rho: -0.7\n519\t    gdn_excluded_LAMBADA_p: 0.233\n520\t    gdn_excluded_ARC_Easy_rho: -0.9\n521\t    gdn_excluded_ARC_Easy_p: 0.083\n522\t    gdn_excluded_MMLU_rho: 0.6\n523\t    gdn_excluded_MMLU_direction: FLIPPED — convergence was GDN-driven artifact\n524\t    MMLU_must_exclude_from_convergence_evidence: true\n525\t  result_rationale: '已完成实验。LAMBADA 不通过 Bonferroni（adj-p=0.100 > 0.0083），BH-FDR 在仅\n526\t    1 个小 p-value 时 无额外收益（也是 0.100）。Bootstrap percentile CI [-1.0, -0.7] 不过零，这是论文的\n527\t    primary statistical argument——方向性确定，只是精确 p-value 在 multi-comparison 下失去显著性。 GDN-excluded\n528\t    分析揭示两个关键发现：(a) ARC-Easy rho 从 -0.7 改善到 -0.9（p=0.083）， 说明 GDN confound 在 ARC-Easy\n529\t    上是噪声源，去除后 convergence signal 更强； (b) MMLU rho 从 -0.7 翻转到 +0.6，MMLU 的 apparent\n530\t    convergence 完全由 GDN 驱动，是 artifact。 这要求 paper 严格标记 MMLU 为 non-convergent。\n531\t\n532\t    '\n533\t  tables:\n534\t  - name: 'Table: Multiple comparison correction (6 benchmarks)'\n535\t    columns:\n536\t    - Benchmark\n537\t    - ρ\n538\t    - Raw p\n539\t    - Bonferroni adj-p\n540\t    - BH-FDR adj-p\n541\t    rows:\n542\t    - - LAMBADA\n543\t      - -1.0\n544\t      - 0.017\n545\t      - 0.1\n546\t      - 0.1\n547\t    - - ARC-Easy\n548\t      - -0.7\n549\t      - 0.233\n550\t      - 1.0\n551\t      - 0.467\n552\t    - - MMLU\n553\t      - -0.7\n554\t      - 0.233\n555\t      - 1.0\n556\t      - 0.467\n557\t    - - ARC-Challenge\n558\t      - 0.6\n559\t      - 0.35\n560\t      - 1.0\n561\t      - 0.525\n562\t    - - HellaSwag\n563\t      - 0.3\n564\t      - 0.683\n565\t      - 1.0\n566\t      - 0.82\n567\t    - - Winogrande\n568\t      - 0.1\n569\t      - 0.95\n570\t      - 1.0\n571\t      - 0.95\n572\t  - name: 'Table: GDN-excluded sensitivity'\n573\t    columns:\n574\t    - Benchmark\n575\t    - Full ρ\n576\t    - GDN-excl ρ\n577\t    - GDN-excl p\n578\t    - Direction\n579\t    rows:\n580\t    - - LAMBADA\n581\t      - -1.0\n582\t      - -0.7\n583\t      - 0.233\n584\t      - Weaker (expected — n drops)\n585\t    - - ARC-Easy\n586\t      - -0.7\n587\t      - -0.9\n588\t      - 0.083\n589\t      - Stronger (confound removed)\n590\t    - - MMLU\n591\t      - -0.7\n592\t      - 0.6\n593\t      - 0.35\n594\t      - ⚠️ FLIPPED — artifact\n595\t  figures_description:\n596\t  - 'Fig: Bootstrap distribution of LAMBADA ρ (10K resamples), with percentile CI\n597\t    marked. 100% of valid resamples have ρ < 0.'\n598\t  analysis: 'Statistical strategy for paper：lead with percentile CI (方向性 certain)，report\n599\t    exact permutation p (transparent)，Bonferroni failure 在 supplementary 诚实报告。GDN-excluded\n600\t    analysis 作为 robustness check， ARC-Easy improvement 作为 additional evidence point。MMLU\n601\t    flipping 是重要 negative result， 必须在 paper 中报告以避免 cherry-picking 指控。\n602\t\n603\t    '\n604\t- name: Wang et al. explicit differentiation\n605\t  plan_id: exp-009\n606\t  description: 与 Wang et al. 的系统性对比，量化 incremental contribution\n607\t  expected_results:\n608\t    differentiation_points: 4\n609\t    wang_no_cross_arch_std_trajectory: true\n610\t    wang_no_per_example_analysis: true\n611\t    wang_no_scale_dependent_convergence: true\n612\t    wang_no_attention_characterization: true\n613\t    wang_qualitative_convergence_mentioned: true\n614\t    wang_exact_quote: models tend to converge in performance as attention ratio increases\n615\t    our_quantification: ρ=-1.0, std 0.024→0.005 (79% reduction), exact permutation\n616\t      p=0.017\n617\t  result_rationale: '已完成实验。Wang et al. 的论文聚焦于 model zoo 的 training recipe 和 architecture\n618\t    comparison， convergence 仅作为 qualitative observation 出现（一句话提及）。他们不计算 cross-arch\n619\t    std trajectories， 不做 per-example analysis，不分析 scale-dependent convergence completeness，不做\n620\t    attention weight characterization。我们的 4-point differentiation 是清晰的。但 Reviewer\n621\t    Concern A 仍需通过 Related Work positioning 来 mitigate——framing 为 \"community analysis\n622\t    enabled by public infrastructure\"。\n623\t\n624\t    '\n625\t  tables:\n626\t  - name: 'Table: Contribution differentiation vs Wang et al.'\n627\t    columns:\n628\t    - Analysis Dimension\n629\t    - Wang et al.\n630\t    - Ours\n631\t    rows:\n632\t    - - Cross-arch std trajectory\n633\t      - Not computed\n634\t      - ρ=-1.0, 79% reduction, permutation p=0.017\n635\t    - - Per-example analysis\n636\t      - Not performed\n637\t      - Jaccard<0.10, KW p=0.0005 (cross-arch)\n638\t    - - Scale-dependent convergence\n639\t      - Not characterized\n640\t      - 'Binary contrast: 1.3B complete, 340M partial rebound'\n641\t    - - Attention characterization\n642\t      - Not performed\n643\t      - Descriptive patterns, cosine sim=0.35\n644\t  figures_description: []\n645\t  analysis: 'Differentiation 清晰且 defensible。关键在于 framing：不是 \"Wang et al. missed this\"\n646\t    而是 \"their public infrastructure enables this analysis, which we contribute.\"\n647\t\n648\t    '\n649\t- name: Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\n650\t  plan_id: exp-010\n651\t  description: 绘制 aggregate convergence 与 per-example divergence 随 attention ratio\n652\t    的 co-evolution\n653\t  expected_results:\n654\t    lambada_attention_ratios:\n655\t    - 0\n656\t    - 3\n657\t    - 6\n658\t    - 12\n659\t    - 24\n660\t    cross_arch_std_trajectory:\n661\t    - 0.024\n662\t    - 0.018\n663\t    - 0.012\n664\t    - 0.008\n665\t    - 0.005\n666\t    mean_pairwise_jaccard_trajectory:\n667\t    - null\n668\t    - 0.09\n669\t    - 0.08\n670\t    - 0.07\n671\t    - 0.06\n672\t    net_effect_asymmetry_trajectory:\n673\t    - null\n674\t    - 0.15\n675\t    - 0.22\n676\t    - 0.28\n677\t    - 0.35\n678\t    convergence_divergence_correlation_rho: -0.95\n679\t    convergence_divergence_correlation_p: 0.05\n680\t    co_evolution_confirmed: true\n681\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下，convergence 和 per-example divergence 的 co-evolution\n682\t    关系成立但统计边缘性。 随着 attention ratio 增加：(1) aggregate std 单调下降（convergence 增强）， (2)\n683\t    pairwise Jaccard 轻微下降（per-example overlap 减少，divergence 增强）， (3) net effect asymmetry\n684\t    增加（每种架构的 \"helped bias\" 越来越不同）。 这三个轨迹在 attention ratio 维度上高度相关（ρ≈-0.95），但 n=4 datapoints（h0\n685\t    无 attention， 无 per-example divergence metric），p=0.05 只是 borderline。 核心 insight：更多\n686\t    attention → aggregate 更 similar，但 per-example mechanism 更 different。 这是 underspecification\n687\t    的具体量化——\"the HOW diverges while the WHAT converges\"。\n688\t\n689\t    '\n690\t  tables:\n691\t  - name: 'Table: Convergence-divergence co-evolution (LAMBADA, 1.3B)'\n692\t    columns:\n693\t    - Attn Ratio\n694\t    - Cross-Arch Std\n695\t    - Mean Jaccard\n696\t    - Effect Asymmetry\n697\t    - N Helped (GDN/RetNet/HGRN2)\n698\t    rows:\n699\t    - - h0 (pure)\n700\t      - 0.024\n701\t      - —\n702\t      - —\n703\t      - —/—/—\n704\t    - - h3\n705\t      - 0.018\n706\t      - 0.09\n707\t      - 0.15\n708\t      - 420/380/490\n709\t    - - h6\n710\t      - 0.012\n711\t      - 0.08\n712\t      - 0.22\n713\t      - 445/410/520\n714\t    - - h12\n715\t      - 0.008\n716\t      - 0.07\n717\t      - 0.28\n718\t      - 460/425/540\n719\t    - - h24\n720\t      - 0.005\n721\t      - 0.06\n722\t      - 0.35\n723\t      - 470/430/555\n724\t  figures_description:\n725\t  - 'Fig (CORE PAPER FIGURE): Dual-axis plot. Left Y = cross-arch std (decreasing),\n726\t    Right Y = effect asymmetry (increasing), X = attention ratio. Two curves crossing\n727\t    — the visual ''scissors'' of convergence-divergence co-evolution.'\n728\t  - 'Fig: Jaccard heatmaps at each attention ratio, showing per-example overlap decreasing\n729\t    as attention increases.'\n730\t  analysis: '这是论文的 signature visualization——一张图讲述整个故事。Aggregate convergence（左轴下降）和\n731\t    per-example divergence（右轴上升）的 \"scissors\" pattern 直观地传达了 underspecification message。\n732\t    统计上 borderline (p=0.05)，paper 用 \"co-evolve\" 而非 \"cause\" 的语言。 在 median 档，这张图足以支撑\n733\t    Findings 论文的核心叙事。\n734\t\n735\t    '\n736\t- name: Additional high-retrieval benchmarks\n737\t  plan_id: exp-011\n738\t  description: 在 StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA 上运行 1.3B 模型，寻找 second convergence anchor\n739\t  expected_results:\n740\t    benchmarks_evaluated:\n741\t    - StoryCloze\n742\t    - BoolQ\n743\t    - COPA\n744\t    StoryCloze:\n745\t      rho: -0.7\n746\t      exact_p_two_tailed: 0.117\n747\t      std_trajectory:\n748\t      - 0.031\n749\t      - 0.025\n750\t      - 0.02\n751\t      - 0.018\n752\t      - 0.015\n753\t      std_reduction_pct: 52\n754\t      direction: consistent with LAMBADA\n755\t      significant: false\n756\t      suggestive: true\n757\t    BoolQ:\n758\t      rho: -0.8\n759\t      exact_p_two_tailed: 0.083\n760\t      std_trajectory:\n761\t      - 0.028\n762\t      - 0.024\n763\t      - 0.018\n764\t      - 0.014\n765\t      - 0.01\n766\t      std_reduction_pct: 64\n767\t      direction: consistent with LAMBADA\n768\t      significant: false\n769\t      suggestive: true\n770\t    COPA:\n771\t      rho: -0.3\n772\t      exact_p_two_tailed: 0.55\n773\t      std_trajectory:\n774\t      - 0.045\n775\t      - 0.042\n776\t      - 0.044\n777\t      - 0.04\n778\t      - 0.038\n779\t      std_reduction_pct: 16\n780\t      direction: weak, inconsistent\n781\t      significant: false\n782\t      suggestive: false\n783\t    best_new_benchmark: BoolQ\n784\t    best_new_rho: -0.8\n785\t    best_new_p: 0.083\n786\t    updated_bh_fdr:\n787\t      LAMBADA_adj_p: 0.075\n788\t      BoolQ_adj_p: 0.375\n789\t      StoryCloze_adj_p: 0.375\n790\t      note: 'BH-FDR with 9 benchmarks: LAMBADA adj-p improves from 0.100 to 0.075\n791\t        but still >0.05; BoolQ does not survive'\n792\t    n_benchmarks_bh_fdr_significant: 1\n793\t    n_suggestive_p_below_0_15: 3\n794\t    gpu_hours_actual: 7\n795\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：最佳新 benchmark (BoolQ) ρ≈-0.8, p≈0.083（suggestive,\n796\t    not significant）。 BoolQ 作为 passage-based yes/no task，其核心操作是从给定 passage 中 retrieve\n797\t    关键信息来判断命题真假， 与 LAMBADA 的 context retrieval 有结构相似性。因此 attention 的 equalizer 效应方向一致。\n798\t    但 BoolQ 的 answer space 是 binary（yes/no），cross-architecture variance 的 baseline\n799\t    本来就低， 加上 n=5 attention ratios 的 power limitation，p 值只能达到 suggestive 水平。 StoryCloze\n800\t    (ρ=-0.7, p=0.117) 也 suggestive——context completion task 的 retrieval 成分支持 convergence\n801\t    方向，但效应弱于 LAMBADA。COPA (ρ=-0.3) 虽名为 causal reasoning from narratives， 实际 sample\n802\t    太短（1-2 sentences），attention 的增量价值小且架构间差异不大。 BH-FDR 在 9 benchmarks 下将 LAMBADA adj-p\n803\t    从 0.100 改善到 0.075——方向好但仍 >0.05， 所以 formal significance 仍然只有 LAMBADA（且仅在 uncorrected\n804\t    下）。 但 3 个 benchmarks (LAMBADA + BoolQ + StoryCloze) 方向一致 + GDN-excluded ARC-Easy\n805\t    (ρ=-0.9, p=0.083) 构成 converging evidence pattern。Paper 的论证从 \"single significant\n806\t    result\" 转为 \"consistent directional pattern across retrieval-heavy tasks\"。\n807\t\n808\t    '\n809\t  tables:\n810\t  - name: 'Table: Extended benchmark convergence analysis (1.3B)'\n811\t    columns:\n812\t    - Benchmark\n813\t    - Task Type\n814\t    - ρ\n815\t    - Exact p (2-tail)\n816\t    - Std Reduction %\n817\t    - Suggestive (p<0.15)?\n818\t    rows:\n819\t    - - LAMBADA\n820\t      - last-word retrieval\n821\t      - -1.0\n822\t      - 0.017\n823\t      - 79%\n824\t      - Yes (significant)\n825\t    - - BoolQ\n826\t      - passage yes/no\n827\t      - -0.8\n828\t      - 0.083\n829\t      - 64%\n830\t      - 'Yes'\n831\t    - - StoryCloze\n832\t      - context completion\n833\t      - -0.7\n834\t      - 0.117\n835\t      - 52%\n836\t      - 'Yes'\n837\t    - - ARC-Easy*\n838\t      - factual QA (GDN-excl)\n839\t      - -0.9\n840\t      - 0.083\n841\t      - —\n842\t      - 'Yes'\n843\t    - - COPA\n844\t      - causal reasoning\n845\t      - -0.3\n846\t      - 0.55\n847\t      - 16%\n848\t      - 'No'\n849\t    - - HellaSwag\n850\t      - commonsense reasoning\n851\t      - 0.3\n852\t      - 0.742\n853\t      - —\n854\t      - 'No'\n855\t    - - ARC-Challenge\n856\t      - multi-step reasoning\n857\t      - 0.6\n858\t      - 0.883\n859\t      - —\n860\t      - 'No'\n861\t    - - Winogrande\n862\t      - coreference reasoning\n863\t      - 0.1\n864\t      - 0.95\n865\t      - —\n866\t      - 'No'\n867\t    - - MMLU†\n868\t      - knowledge QA\n869\t      - —\n870\t      - —\n871\t      - —\n872\t      - Excluded (GDN artifact)\n873\t  - name: 'Table: Updated BH-FDR correction (9 benchmarks)'\n874\t    columns:\n875\t    - Rank\n876\t    - Benchmark\n877\t    - Raw p\n878\t    - BH threshold\n879\t    - BH adj-p\n880\t    - Significant?\n881\t    rows:\n882\t    - - 1\n883\t      - LAMBADA\n884\t      - 0.017\n885\t      - 0.006\n886\t      - 0.075\n887\t      - No (improved from 0.100)\n888\t    - - 2\n889\t      - BoolQ\n890\t      - 0.083\n891\t      - 0.011\n892\t      - 0.375\n893\t      - 'No'\n894\t    - - 3\n895\t      - ARC-Easy\n896\t      - 0.117\n897\t      - 0.017\n898\t      - 0.375\n899\t      - 'No'\n900\t    - - 4\n901\t      - StoryCloze\n902\t      - 0.117\n903\t      - 0.022\n904\t      - 0.375\n905\t      - 'No'\n906\t    - - 5\n907\t      - ARC-Challenge\n908\t      - 0.35\n909\t      - 0.028\n910\t      - 0.63\n911\t      - 'No'\n912\t    - - 6\n913\t      - COPA\n914\t      - 0.55\n915\t      - 0.033\n916\t      - 0.825\n917\t      - 'No'\n918\t    - - 7\n919\t      - HellaSwag\n920\t      - 0.683\n921\t      - 0.039\n922\t      - 0.878\n923\t      - 'No'\n924\t    - - 8\n925\t      - Winogrande\n926\t      - 0.95\n927\t      - 0.044\n928\t      - 0.95\n929\t      - 'No'\n930\t    - - 9\n931\t      - MMLU\n932\t      - excl\n933\t      - —\n934\t      - —\n935\t      - Excluded\n936\t  figures_description:\n937\t  - 'Fig: Forest plot of convergence ρ across all benchmarks, ordered by retrieval\n938\t    demand. Clear gradient: high-retrieval tasks cluster at negative ρ, reasoning\n939\t    tasks at zero/positive.'\n940\t  - 'Fig: Std reduction trajectories for LAMBADA + BoolQ + StoryCloze (converging)\n941\t    vs HellaSwag + ARC-C + COPA (flat/diverging), showing task-type dichotomy.'\n942\t  analysis: Exp-011 在 median 档下不产生 second significant anchor（BH-FDR 仍仅 LAMBADA 在 uncorrected\n943\t    下显著）， 但产生有价值的 converging evidence pattern。Paper 的 statistical argument 变为： \"While\n944\t    no single additional benchmark reaches significance after correction, the consistent\n945\t    negative direction across retrieval-heavy tasks (LAMBADA ρ=-1.0, BoolQ ρ=-0.8,\n946\t    StoryCloze ρ=-0.7, GDN-excluded ARC-Easy ρ=-0.9) versus null/positive results\n947\t    on reasoning tasks suggests the convergence effect is systematically related to\n948\t    task type rather than a LAMBADA-specific artifact.\" 这是 honest framing——不 overclaim\n949\t    significance，但通过 direction consistency + task taxonomy 构建 reasonable evidence。对\n950\t    EMNLP Findings 足够，但 Main 困难。\n951\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5f8c2b8-a1ca-4a4a-8211-80150d29dabf","uuid":"04e5df95-50c6-4899-85c1-4bab6df7b1fc","timestamp":"2026-05-19T15:31:15.050Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_2/projects/entrainment_gated_ft/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260519T143201/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Claim 1 弱化为 ''convergence on retrieval-heavy tasks with suggestive\n  evidence on related benchmarks''。 LAMBADA 仍为唯一 BH-FDR 显著锚点，但 exp-011 新 benchmark\n  方向一致性 + GDN-excluded ARC-Easy 改善 构成 converging evidence pattern。exp-004 以描述性证据呈现，避免\n  mechanistic language。 exp-005 未扩展架构数量。exp-007 部分解释 340M rebound 但留有未解问题。 Claim 3\n  per-example divergence 成为论文相对最强的独立贡献。目标 EMNLP Findings，honest framing。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Task-specificity characterization of equalizer effect\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: 计算 6 个 benchmark 在每个 attention ratio 下的 cross-architecture std，建立 task\n    taxonomy\n  expected_results:\n    LAMBADA_rho: -1.0\n    LAMBADA_p: 0.008\n    LAMBADA_taxonomy: retrieval-dependent\n    LAMBADA_std_reduction_pct: 79\n    HellaSwag_rho: 0.3\n    HellaSwag_p: 0.742\n    HellaSwag_taxonomy: reasoning-dependent\n    ARC_Challenge_rho: 0.6\n    ARC_Challenge_p: 0.883\n    ARC_Challenge_taxonomy: reasoning-dependent\n    Winogrande_rho: 0.1\n    Winogrande_p: 0.608\n    Winogrande_taxonomy: reasoning-dependent\n    ARC_Easy_rho: -0.7\n    ARC_Easy_p: 0.117\n    ARC_Easy_taxonomy: mixed\n    MMLU_rho: -0.7\n    MMLU_p: 0.117\n    MMLU_taxonomy: mixed\n    significant_count: 1/6\n  result_rationale: '已完成实验。LAMBADA 作为 last-word-in-context retrieval task，attention\n    直接增强了从上文提取目标词的能力， 且三种架构的 baseline 缺陷高度同质（都缺少 global attention），因此 attention 的补偿效应方向一致、\n    幅度相近，产生强 convergence。Reasoning tasks (HellaSwag, ARC-C, Winogrande) 依赖多步推理链， attention\n    的增益是架构特异性的（不同 recurrent backbone 的 bottleneck 不同），所以不 converge。 ARC-Easy 和 MMLU\n    介于两者之间：含部分 retrieval 成分但也需要 world knowledge，产生 suggestive 但不显著的趋势。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table 1: Task-specificity of convergence effect'\n    columns:\n    - Benchmark\n    - Task Type\n    - ρ (Spearman)\n    - p (exact perm.)\n    - Std Reduction %\n    - Taxonomy\n    rows:\n    - - LAMBADA\n      - last-word retrieval\n      - -1.0\n      - 0.008\n      - 79%\n      - retrieval-dependent\n    - - ARC-Easy\n      - factual QA\n      - -0.7\n      - 0.117\n      - 42%\n      - mixed\n    - - MMLU\n      - knowledge QA\n      - -0.7\n      - 0.117\n      - 38%\n      - mixed\n    - - HellaSwag\n      - commonsense reasoning\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.742\n      - +15%\n      - reasoning-dependent\n    - - Winogrande\n      - coreference reasoning\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.608\n      - +8%\n      - reasoning-dependent\n    - - ARC-Challenge\n      - multi-step reasoning\n      - 0.6\n      - 0.883\n      - +22%\n      - reasoning-dependent\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig 1: 6-panel grid, 每个 benchmark 一个 panel。X 轴 = attention ratio (h0→h24), Y\n    轴 = cross-arch std。LAMBADA panel 展示清晰下降趋势，reasoning tasks 平坦或上升。'\n  analysis: 'Taxonomy 清晰分为三档：retrieval-dependent (LAMBADA, 强 convergence)、mixed (ARC-Easy/MMLU,\n    suggestive)、 reasoning-dependent (HellaSwag/Winogrande/ARC-C, 无 convergence 或反向)。这支持\n    attention 的 equalizer 效应是 task-modulated 的解释——当 task 的关键 bottleneck 恰好是 global\n    context retrieval 时， attention 对所有架构提供相似的补偿。\n\n    '\n- name: Multi-benchmark per-example analysis\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: 对 HellaSwag/ARC-Easy/ARC-Challenge 收集 --log_samples per-example 数据，验证\n    task-specificity 在 per-example 层面的表现\n  expected_results:\n    n_models_rerun: 13\n    models_340m:\n    - RetNet×5\n    - HGRN2×5\n    models_1_3b:\n    - GDN h3-1\n    - GDN h6-1\n    - GDN h24-1\n    HellaSwag_per_example_n: 10042\n    ARC_Easy_per_example_n: 2376\n    ARC_Challenge_per_example_n: 1172\n    HellaSwag_cross_arch_jaccard_helped: 0.18\n    HellaSwag_cross_arch_jaccard_hurt: 0.15\n    ARC_Easy_cross_arch_jaccard_helped: 0.14\n    ARC_Easy_cross_arch_jaccard_hurt: 0.11\n    ARC_Challenge_cross_arch_jaccard_helped: 0.12\n    ARC_Challenge_cross_arch_jaccard_hurt: 0.1\n    LAMBADA_reference_jaccard: 0.08\n    task_specificity_per_example_confirmed: true\n    reasoning_task_pattern: systematic_but_architecture_specific\n    gpu_hours_actual: 18\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下，per-example 数据成功收集但揭示了 nuanced pattern：reasoning tasks\n    的 per-example Jaccard 比 LAMBADA 高（0.10-0.18 vs 0.05-0.10），说明 attention 在 reasoning\n    tasks 上影响的样本集有更多重叠， 但这种重叠并不 translate 为 aggregate convergence（因为影响方向和幅度是架构特异的）。\n    LAMBADA 的低 Jaccard 反而说明：aggregate convergence 不是因为 attention 帮助了相同的样本， 而是因为不同样本的帮助在\n    aggregate 层面恰好相互补偿到相似水平。 这加强了 Claim 3 的 underspecification 叙事——convergence 和 per-example\n    agreement 是正交的维度。 Reasoning tasks 展示 \"systematic but architecture-specific\" pattern：每个架构内\n    helped/hurt 有结构性， 但跨架构差异大到无法 aggregate converge。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Per-example overlap (Jaccard) across benchmarks at h3-1, 1.3B'\n    columns:\n    - Benchmark\n    - Jaccard (helped)\n    - Jaccard (hurt)\n    - LAMBADA ref.\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - LAMBADA\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.07\n      - —\n      - Low overlap → different samples helped per arch\n    - - HellaSwag\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.15\n      - 2.3×\n      - Higher overlap but no aggregate convergence\n    - - ARC-Easy\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.11\n      - 1.8×\n      - Moderate overlap, suggestive convergence\n    - - ARC-Challenge\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.1\n      - 1.5×\n      - Moderate overlap, no convergence\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Jaccard heatmap (3 arch pairs × 4 benchmarks), 颜色编码 per-example overlap。LAMBADA\n    行最冷（低 overlap），HellaSwag 行最暖。'\n  - 'Fig: Per-example effect scatter (baseline ppl vs Δ accuracy) for each benchmark\n    × architecture，展示 reasoning tasks 的架构特异性 pattern。'\n  analysis: 'Per-example 数据确认 task-specificity 不仅存在于 aggregate 层面，也存在于 per-example\n    层面，但方式不同于预期。 Reasoning tasks 有更高的 per-example overlap（attention 倾向于影响某些 \"universally\n    tricky\" 样本）， 但影响的方向和幅度架构特异。LAMBADA 的低 overlap + 高 aggregate convergence 构成最强的\n    underspecification 案例。 exp-002 的结论：Claim 1 的 task-specificity 在 per-example 层面同样成立但机制更复杂；\n    Claim 3 的 per-example divergence 在 LAMBADA 上最极端，但在所有 tasks 上都存在（程度不同）。\n\n    '\n- name: Attention weight extraction and visualization\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: 提取 3 种架构 h3-1 配置的 attention weights，分析与 helped/hurt sample 的关联\n  expected_results:\n    n_models_analyzed: 3\n    attention_configs: h3-1 (1 attention layer in 3-layer block)\n    n_lambada_samples_analyzed: 500\n    attn_entropy_GDN_mean: 3.42\n    attn_entropy_RetNet_mean: 3.18\n    attn_entropy_HGRN2_mean: 3.55\n    attn_pattern_helped_hurt_correlation_GDN: 0.22\n    attn_pattern_helped_hurt_correlation_RetNet: 0.18\n    attn_pattern_helped_hurt_correlation_HGRN2: 0.25\n    mean_attn_effect_correlation: 0.22\n    cross_arch_attn_similarity_cosine: 0.35\n    attn_focus_last_sentence_pct_GDN: 62\n    attn_focus_last_sentence_pct_RetNet: 55\n    attn_focus_last_sentence_pct_HGRN2: 58\n    helped_vs_hurt_attn_entropy_diff_p: 0.08\n    gpu_hours_actual: 3.5\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下，attention-effect correlation 落在 0.15-0.30 区间（实际均值 0.22）。\n    这不足以做 strong mechanistic claim，但足以做描述性报告。原因： (1) attention weights 只是 model 行为的\n    partial view——per-example 效果由 attention + recurrent backbone 的交互决定，单看 attention\n    只能捕获部分 variance。 (2) h3-1 配置仅 1 层 attention（在 3 层 block 中），信息密度有限。 (3) 不同架构的 attention\n    确实 focus 在不同位置（cross-arch cosine similarity 仅 0.35）， 这与 per-example divergence\n    一致——架构之间 attention 的 \"关注点\" 不同。 (4) 所有架构的 attention 都倾向于 focus on last sentence（55-62%），这与\n    LAMBADA 的 retrieval nature 一致， 但具体 token-level focus 差异显著。 Helped 样本的 attention\n    entropy 略低于 hurt 样本（p=0.08），暗示 attention 在 \"知道该看哪里\" 时更有效， 但这只是 suggestive。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Attention pattern statistics by architecture (h3-1, 1.3B, LAMBADA)'\n    columns:\n    - Architecture\n    - Mean Entropy\n    - Last-Sentence Focus %\n    - Helped-Hurt Corr.\n    - Helped Entropy\n    - Hurt Entropy\n    rows:\n    - - GDN\n      - 3.42\n      - 62%\n      - 0.22\n      - 3.31\n      - 3.52\n    - - RetNet\n      - 3.18\n      - 55%\n      - 0.18\n      - 3.1\n      - 3.28\n    - - HGRN2\n      - 3.55\n      - 58%\n      - 0.25\n      - 3.42\n      - 3.65\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-architecture attention similarity'\n    columns:\n    - Arch Pair\n    - Cosine Sim (mean attn)\n    - Cosine Sim (helped subset)\n    - Cosine Sim (hurt subset)\n    rows:\n    - - GDN–RetNet\n      - 0.33\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.31\n    - - GDN–HGRN2\n      - 0.38\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.33\n    - - RetNet–HGRN2\n      - 0.34\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.29\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Attention heatmap (3 panels, one per arch) on 5 representative LAMBADA examples,\n    showing divergent focus patterns across architectures on the same input.'\n  - 'Fig: Scatter plot of per-sample attention entropy vs Δ accuracy for each architecture.\n    Weak negative trend (r≈0.18-0.25) with wide scatter.'\n  analysis: 'Attention patterns 确认三种架构的 attention 在 same input 上 focus 不同位置（cosine\n    sim ≈ 0.35）， 这与 per-example Jaccard < 0.10 一致。但 attention-effect correlation 仅\n    0.22，不足以说 \"attention pattern 决定了 which samples are helped\"——只能说 \"attention patterns\n    differ across architectures on affected samples\"。Paper 中以描述性语言呈现：\"We observe that\n    attention allocation patterns diverge across architectures (mean cosine similarity\n    = 0.35), consistent with the per-example divergence reported in Section X. However,\n    the modest correlation between attention statistics and per-example effects (r\n    = 0.22) suggests that attention weights alone do not fully account for the architecture-specific\n    patterns.\" 避免 \"mechanistic\" 一词。\n\n    '\n- name: Architecture expansion check\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 搜索 Wang et al. model zoo 和其他来源，寻找额外 hybrid 架构（Mamba hybrids, RWKV hybrids\n    等）\n  expected_results:\n    additional_architectures_found: 0\n    wang_et_al_architectures_checked:\n    - GatedDeltaNet\n    - RetNet\n    - HGRN2\n    - DeltaNet\n    - RWKV6\n    - Mamba\n    hybrid_configs_available:\n    - GatedDeltaNet\n    - RetNet\n    - HGRN2\n    non_hybrid_only:\n    - DeltaNet\n    - RWKV6\n    - Mamba\n    reason_no_expansion: Wang et al. model zoo 中只有 GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 有 attention-hybrid\n      配置；DeltaNet/RWKV6/Mamba 仅有 pure recurrent。外部无 compatible hybrid checkpoints。\n    n_architectures_final: 3\n    gpu_hours_actual: 0\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：exp-005 未找到可评估的额外架构。 Wang et al. 的 model zoo 设计上只为\n    GDN/RetNet/HGRN2 提供了 hybrid (attention-augmented) 配置， 因为这三种是他们论文的重点对比对象。DeltaNet、RWKV6、Mamba\n    等只有 pure recurrent checkpoints， 没有对应的 hybrid variants。外部开源社区（HuggingFace、GitHub）的\n    hybrid checkpoints 要么训练设置不同 （不同数据、不同 tokenizer），要么规模不匹配，无法做 controlled comparison。\n    因此 n=3 架构是硬限制。Paper 在 Limitations 中诚实说明：\"Our analysis is limited to three architectures\n    with publicly available hybrid configurations. Extending to Mamba-2 or RWKV-6\n    hybrids requires training new models, which we leave to future work.\"\n\n    '\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: '未产生新数据。n=3 限制通过两种方式 mitigate： (1) 论证 3 architectures × 5 attention ratios\n    × 2 scales = 30 model configurations 提供了足够的统计结构； (2) per-example analysis 提供 5153\n    data points per pairwise comparison，补偿了架构数量的不足。 Reviewer Concern D 的回应策略不变。\n\n    '\n- name: 7B model evaluation — CANCELLED\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: 7B 模型不可用，已取消。预算重新分配。\n  expected_results:\n    status: cancelled\n    reason: Wang et al. 仅提供 340M + 1.3B (72 models total)\n  result_rationale: Wang et al. model zoo 不包含 7B 规模模型。无外部可比较的 hybrid 7B checkpoints。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 预算重新分配给 exp-002 和 exp-004。Claim 2 限制为 binary scale contrast。\n- name: 340M rebound mechanism analysis\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: 分析 340M 在 attn=8 处的 non-monotonic rebound，与 1.3B 做 per-example 对比\n  expected_results:\n    rebound_attention_ratio: h8 (8/24 attention layers)\n    rebound_magnitude_std_increase: 35-40% relative to h6 minimum\n    n_rebound_samples_340m: 280\n    n_rebound_samples_overlap_with_1_3b_hurt: 95\n    overlap_pct: 34\n    rebound_sample_characteristics:\n      mean_context_length: 42.3\n      mean_target_frequency_rank: 8500\n      mean_baseline_ppl: 4.8\n    partial_explanation_pct: 60\n    capacity_saturation_hypothesis: supported_but_not_conclusive\n    training_tokens_confound: acknowledged_not_resolved\n    arch_specific_rebound:\n      GDN_340m_rebound: moderate (std +30%)\n      RetNet_340m_rebound: strong (std +55%)\n      HGRN2_340m_rebound: weak (std +20%)\n    gpu_hours_actual: 2\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：340M rebound 可部分解释但非完全清晰。 部分解释（~60%）：340M 模型在 h8\n    ratio 时，attention 层数已占 1/3 的 model capacity， 对于小模型来说 attention 的参数开销（QKV projections）挤占了\n    recurrent backbone 的表达能力， 导致某些样本从 \"helped by attention\" 回退到 \"hurt by capacity\n    reallocation\"。 具体表现为：rebound 样本与 1.3B 的 hurt 样本有 34% 重叠——这些是 \"需要 attention 但也需要\n    足够 recurrent capacity 来编码上下文\" 的样本。1.3B 有足够 capacity 同时支持两者。 未解释部分（~40%）：不同架构的\n    rebound 幅度差异大（RetNet 最强 +55%，HGRN2 最弱 +20%）， 暗示 rebound 不仅是 capacity issue，还与\n    backbone 的 inductive bias 有关。 训练 token 数量差异（340M: 20B tokens, 1.3B: 100B tokens）作为\n    confound 被承认但无法分离—— 需要 controlled training runs 才能解开，超出本文 scope。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: 340M rebound characterization by architecture'\n    columns:\n    - Architecture\n    - h6 Std\n    - h8 Std\n    - Rebound %\n    - N Rebound Samples\n    - Overlap with 1.3B Hurt %\n    rows:\n    - - GDN\n      - 0.018\n      - 0.023\n      - +30%\n      - 85\n      - 38%\n    - - RetNet\n      - 0.015\n      - 0.023\n      - +55%\n      - 120\n      - 31%\n    - - HGRN2\n      - 0.02\n      - 0.024\n      - +20%\n      - 75\n      - 33%\n  - name: 'Table: Rebound sample characteristics vs non-rebound'\n    columns:\n    - Feature\n    - Rebound Samples\n    - Non-Rebound\n    - p (MW-U)\n    rows:\n    - - Context length (tokens)\n      - 42.3\n      - 35.1\n      - 0.03\n    - - Target freq rank\n      - 8500\n      - 6200\n      - 0.07\n    - - Baseline ppl (340M)\n      - 4.8\n      - 3.5\n      - 0.01\n    - - Baseline ppl (1.3B)\n      - 3.1\n      - 2.8\n      - 0.22\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Cross-arch std trajectory at 340M showing non-monotonic rebound at h8, with\n    1.3B monotonic curve overlaid for contrast.'\n  - 'Fig: Venn diagram of rebound samples at 340M vs hurt samples at 1.3B, showing\n    34% overlap.'\n  analysis: 'Binary contrast narrative：1.3B 的 monotonic convergence vs 340M 的 non-monotonic\n    rebound 表明 \"convergence requires sufficient capacity\"。Rebound 样本是 \"harder\" samples（higher\n    baseline ppl, longer context），这些样本在 340M 下面临 capacity-attention tradeoff。 Paper\n    framing：\"The non-monotonic pattern at 340M suggests a capacity threshold: smaller\n    models face a tradeoff between recurrent backbone capacity and attention coverage,\n    with the rebound at h8 disproportionately affecting longer-context, higher-difficulty\n    examples (baseline ppl 4.8 vs 3.5, p=0.01).\" 诚实承认：training token confound 和 architecture-specific\n    rebound variance 未完全解释。 这足以支持 Claim 2 的 binary contrast framing，但不足以做 extrapolation\n    或 general scaling law claim。\n\n    '\n- name: Helped/hurt sample characterization\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: 分析 LAMBADA 上每种架构的 helped/hurt 样本特征（surface features + perplexity）\n  expected_results:\n    phase1_surface_features:\n      GDN_helped: 462\n      GDN_hurt: 615\n      GDN_surface_significant: false\n      HGRN2_helped: 548\n      HGRN2_hurt: 395\n      HGRN2_surface_significant: false\n      RetNet_helped: 426\n      RetNet_hurt: 495\n      RetNet_context_length_p: 0.012\n      RetNet_context_length_r: -0.096\n      RetNet_unique_tokens_p: 0.009\n      RetNet_unique_tokens_r: -0.099\n      cross_arch_difference_significant: false\n    phase2_perplexity:\n      GDN_r_rb: -0.04\n      GDN_p: 0.209\n      RetNet_r_rb: -0.02\n      RetNet_p: 0.659\n      HGRN2_r_rb: -0.04\n      HGRN2_p: 0.248\n      within_arch_significant: false\n      cross_arch_hurt_KW_p: 0.0005\n      cross_arch_helped_KW_p: 0.02\n  result_rationale: '已完成实验。Within-architecture：surface features 和 baseline perplexity\n    均无法区分 helped/hurt 样本（所有 within-arch p > 0.2，effect size 极小）。这 rules out trivial\n    explanations—— 不是简单的 \"长句子被 attention 帮助\" 或 \"难样本被帮助\"。 Cross-architecture：不同架构 hurt\n    的样本有 systematically different baseline difficulty profiles (KW p=0.0005)。这表明每种架构\n    \"struggle with\" 不同难度分布的样本，attention 帮助/伤害的样本 子集因此不同。这是 structured diversity, not\n    random noise——支持 Claim 3。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Within-architecture perplexity analysis'\n    columns:\n    - Architecture\n    - Helped Mean PPL\n    - Hurt Mean PPL\n    - U statistic\n    - p\n    - r_rb\n    rows:\n    - - GDN\n      - 3.37\n      - 3.34\n      - 148410\n      - 0.209\n      - -0.045\n    - - RetNet\n      - 3.44\n      - 3.42\n      - 107210\n      - 0.659\n      - -0.017\n    - - HGRN2\n      - 3.38\n      - 3.35\n      - 112999\n      - 0.248\n      - -0.044\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-architecture Kruskal-Wallis tests'\n    columns:\n    - Sample Type\n    - KW H\n    - p\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - Hurt samples\n      - —\n      - 0.0005\n      - Architectures hurt samples with different difficulty profiles\n    - - Helped samples\n      - —\n      - 0.02\n      - Weaker but significant cross-arch difference\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Violin plots of baseline perplexity distributions for hurt samples, split\n    by architecture. Visually distinct distributions despite non-significant within-arch\n    effects.'\n  analysis: 'Two-level finding：(1) within-arch opacity (attention effects 无法用 surface\n    features/perplexity 预测)， (2) cross-arch structure (不同架构的 affected samples 有 systematically\n    different profiles)。 这同时加强 Claim 3 的两个方面——divergence 不是 random noise（structured），\n    但也不是 trivially predictable（opaque to standard features）。\n\n    '\n- name: Statistical robustness framework\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: Bootstrap CIs、multiple comparison correction、GDN-excluded sensitivity\n    analysis\n  expected_results:\n    LAMBADA_rho: -1.0\n    LAMBADA_exact_p_two_tailed: 0.0167\n    LAMBADA_bonferroni_adj_p: 0.1\n    LAMBADA_bh_fdr_adj_p: 0.1\n    bootstrap_ci_lower: -1.0\n    bootstrap_ci_upper: -0.7\n    bootstrap_ci_crosses_zero: false\n    bootstrap_n_valid: 8875\n    bootstrap_n_total: 10000\n    bca_degenerate: true\n    gdn_excluded_LAMBADA_rho: -0.7\n    gdn_excluded_LAMBADA_p: 0.233\n    gdn_excluded_ARC_Easy_rho: -0.9\n    gdn_excluded_ARC_Easy_p: 0.083\n    gdn_excluded_MMLU_rho: 0.6\n    gdn_excluded_MMLU_direction: FLIPPED — convergence was GDN-driven artifact\n    MMLU_must_exclude_from_convergence_evidence: true\n  result_rationale: '已完成实验。LAMBADA 不通过 Bonferroni（adj-p=0.100 > 0.0083），BH-FDR 在仅\n    1 个小 p-value 时 无额外收益（也是 0.100）。Bootstrap percentile CI [-1.0, -0.7] 不过零，这是论文的\n    primary statistical argument——方向性确定，只是精确 p-value 在 multi-comparison 下失去显著性。 GDN-excluded\n    分析揭示两个关键发现：(a) ARC-Easy rho 从 -0.7 改善到 -0.9（p=0.083）， 说明 GDN confound 在 ARC-Easy\n    上是噪声源，去除后 convergence signal 更强； (b) MMLU rho 从 -0.7 翻转到 +0.6，MMLU 的 apparent\n    convergence 完全由 GDN 驱动，是 artifact。 这要求 paper 严格标记 MMLU 为 non-convergent。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Multiple comparison correction (6 benchmarks)'\n    columns:\n    - Benchmark\n    - ρ\n    - Raw p\n    - Bonferroni adj-p\n    - BH-FDR adj-p\n    rows:\n    - - LAMBADA\n      - -1.0\n      - 0.017\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.1\n    - - ARC-Easy\n      - -0.7\n      - 0.233\n      - 1.0\n      - 0.467\n    - - MMLU\n      - -0.7\n      - 0.233\n      - 1.0\n      - 0.467\n    - - ARC-Challenge\n      - 0.6\n      - 0.35\n      - 1.0\n      - 0.525\n    - - HellaSwag\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.683\n      - 1.0\n      - 0.82\n    - - Winogrande\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.95\n      - 1.0\n      - 0.95\n  - name: 'Table: GDN-excluded sensitivity'\n    columns:\n    - Benchmark\n    - Full ρ\n    - GDN-excl ρ\n    - GDN-excl p\n    - Direction\n    rows:\n    - - LAMBADA\n      - -1.0\n      - -0.7\n      - 0.233\n      - Weaker (expected — n drops)\n    - - ARC-Easy\n      - -0.7\n      - -0.9\n      - 0.083\n      - Stronger (confound removed)\n    - - MMLU\n      - -0.7\n      - 0.6\n      - 0.35\n      - ⚠️ FLIPPED — artifact\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Bootstrap distribution of LAMBADA ρ (10K resamples), with percentile CI\n    marked. 100% of valid resamples have ρ < 0.'\n  analysis: 'Statistical strategy for paper：lead with percentile CI (方向性 certain)，report\n    exact permutation p (transparent)，Bonferroni failure 在 supplementary 诚实报告。GDN-excluded\n    analysis 作为 robustness check， ARC-Easy improvement 作为 additional evidence point。MMLU\n    flipping 是重要 negative result， 必须在 paper 中报告以避免 cherry-picking 指控。\n\n    '\n- name: Wang et al. explicit differentiation\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 与 Wang et al. 的系统性对比，量化 incremental contribution\n  expected_results:\n    differentiation_points: 4\n    wang_no_cross_arch_std_trajectory: true\n    wang_no_per_example_analysis: true\n    wang_no_scale_dependent_convergence: true\n    wang_no_attention_characterization: true\n    wang_qualitative_convergence_mentioned: true\n    wang_exact_quote: models tend to converge in performance as attention ratio increases\n    our_quantification: ρ=-1.0, std 0.024→0.005 (79% reduction), exact permutation\n      p=0.017\n  result_rationale: '已完成实验。Wang et al. 的论文聚焦于 model zoo 的 training recipe 和 architecture\n    comparison， convergence 仅作为 qualitative observation 出现（一句话提及）。他们不计算 cross-arch\n    std trajectories， 不做 per-example analysis，不分析 scale-dependent convergence completeness，不做\n    attention weight characterization。我们的 4-point differentiation 是清晰的。但 Reviewer\n    Concern A 仍需通过 Related Work positioning 来 mitigate——framing 为 \"community analysis\n    enabled by public infrastructure\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Contribution differentiation vs Wang et al.'\n    columns:\n    - Analysis Dimension\n    - Wang et al.\n    - Ours\n    rows:\n    - - Cross-arch std trajectory\n      - Not computed\n      - ρ=-1.0, 79% reduction, permutation p=0.017\n    - - Per-example analysis\n      - Not performed\n      - Jaccard<0.10, KW p=0.0005 (cross-arch)\n    - - Scale-dependent convergence\n      - Not characterized\n      - 'Binary contrast: 1.3B complete, 340M partial rebound'\n    - - Attention characterization\n      - Not performed\n      - Descriptive patterns, cosine sim=0.35\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Differentiation 清晰且 defensible。关键在于 framing：不是 \"Wang et al. missed this\"\n    而是 \"their public infrastructure enables this analysis, which we contribute.\"\n\n    '\n- name: Convergence-divergence bridge analysis\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: 绘制 aggregate convergence 与 per-example divergence 随 attention ratio\n    的 co-evolution\n  expected_results:\n    lambada_attention_ratios:\n    - 0\n    - 3\n    - 6\n    - 12\n    - 24\n    cross_arch_std_trajectory:\n    - 0.024\n    - 0.018\n    - 0.012\n    - 0.008\n    - 0.005\n    mean_pairwise_jaccard_trajectory:\n    - null\n    - 0.09\n    - 0.08\n    - 0.07\n    - 0.06\n    net_effect_asymmetry_trajectory:\n    - null\n    - 0.15\n    - 0.22\n    - 0.28\n    - 0.35\n    convergence_divergence_correlation_rho: -0.95\n    convergence_divergence_correlation_p: 0.05\n    co_evolution_confirmed: true\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下，convergence 和 per-example divergence 的 co-evolution\n    关系成立但统计边缘性。 随着 attention ratio 增加：(1) aggregate std 单调下降（convergence 增强）， (2)\n    pairwise Jaccard 轻微下降（per-example overlap 减少，divergence 增强）， (3) net effect asymmetry\n    增加（每种架构的 \"helped bias\" 越来越不同）。 这三个轨迹在 attention ratio 维度上高度相关（ρ≈-0.95），但 n=4 datapoints（h0\n    无 attention， 无 per-example divergence metric），p=0.05 只是 borderline。 核心 insight：更多\n    attention → aggregate 更 similar，但 per-example mechanism 更 different。 这是 underspecification\n    的具体量化——\"the HOW diverges while the WHAT converges\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Convergence-divergence co-evolution (LAMBADA, 1.3B)'\n    columns:\n    - Attn Ratio\n    - Cross-Arch Std\n    - Mean Jaccard\n    - Effect Asymmetry\n    - N Helped (GDN/RetNet/HGRN2)\n    rows:\n    - - h0 (pure)\n      - 0.024\n      - —\n      - —\n      - —/—/—\n    - - h3\n      - 0.018\n      - 0.09\n      - 0.15\n      - 420/380/490\n    - - h6\n      - 0.012\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.22\n      - 445/410/520\n    - - h12\n      - 0.008\n      - 0.07\n      - 0.28\n      - 460/425/540\n    - - h24\n      - 0.005\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.35\n      - 470/430/555\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig (CORE PAPER FIGURE): Dual-axis plot. Left Y = cross-arch std (decreasing),\n    Right Y = effect asymmetry (increasing), X = attention ratio. Two curves crossing\n    — the visual ''scissors'' of convergence-divergence co-evolution.'\n  - 'Fig: Jaccard heatmaps at each attention ratio, showing per-example overlap decreasing\n    as attention increases.'\n  analysis: '这是论文的 signature visualization——一张图讲述整个故事。Aggregate convergence（左轴下降）和\n    per-example divergence（右轴上升）的 \"scissors\" pattern 直观地传达了 underspecification message。\n    统计上 borderline (p=0.05)，paper 用 \"co-evolve\" 而非 \"cause\" 的语言。 在 median 档，这张图足以支撑\n    Findings 论文的核心叙事。\n\n    '\n- name: Additional high-retrieval benchmarks\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: 在 StoryCloze/BoolQ/COPA 上运行 1.3B 模型，寻找 second convergence anchor\n  expected_results:\n    benchmarks_evaluated:\n    - StoryCloze\n    - BoolQ\n    - COPA\n    StoryCloze:\n      rho: -0.7\n      exact_p_two_tailed: 0.117\n      std_trajectory:\n      - 0.031\n      - 0.025\n      - 0.02\n      - 0.018\n      - 0.015\n      std_reduction_pct: 52\n      direction: consistent with LAMBADA\n      significant: false\n      suggestive: true\n    BoolQ:\n      rho: -0.8\n      exact_p_two_tailed: 0.083\n      std_trajectory:\n      - 0.028\n      - 0.024\n      - 0.018\n      - 0.014\n      - 0.01\n      std_reduction_pct: 64\n      direction: consistent with LAMBADA\n      significant: false\n      suggestive: true\n    COPA:\n      rho: -0.3\n      exact_p_two_tailed: 0.55\n      std_trajectory:\n      - 0.045\n      - 0.042\n      - 0.044\n      - 0.04\n      - 0.038\n      std_reduction_pct: 16\n      direction: weak, inconsistent\n      significant: false\n      suggestive: false\n    best_new_benchmark: BoolQ\n    best_new_rho: -0.8\n    best_new_p: 0.083\n    updated_bh_fdr:\n      LAMBADA_adj_p: 0.075\n      BoolQ_adj_p: 0.375\n      StoryCloze_adj_p: 0.375\n      note: 'BH-FDR with 9 benchmarks: LAMBADA adj-p improves from 0.100 to 0.075\n        but still >0.05; BoolQ does not survive'\n    n_benchmarks_bh_fdr_significant: 1\n    n_suggestive_p_below_0_15: 3\n    gpu_hours_actual: 7\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：最佳新 benchmark (BoolQ) ρ≈-0.8, p≈0.083（suggestive,\n    not significant）。 BoolQ 作为 passage-based yes/no task，其核心操作是从给定 passage 中 retrieve\n    关键信息来判断命题真假， 与 LAMBADA 的 context retrieval 有结构相似性。因此 attention 的 equalizer 效应方向一致。\n    但 BoolQ 的 answer space 是 binary（yes/no），cross-architecture variance 的 baseline\n    本来就低， 加上 n=5 attention ratios 的 power limitation，p 值只能达到 suggestive 水平。 StoryCloze\n    (ρ=-0.7, p=0.117) 也 suggestive——context completion task 的 retrieval 成分支持 convergence\n    方向，但效应弱于 LAMBADA。COPA (ρ=-0.3) 虽名为 causal reasoning from narratives， 实际 sample\n    太短（1-2 sentences），attention 的增量价值小且架构间差异不大。 BH-FDR 在 9 benchmarks 下将 LAMBADA adj-p\n    从 0.100 改善到 0.075——方向好但仍 >0.05， 所以 formal significance 仍然只有 LAMBADA（且仅在 uncorrected\n    下）。 但 3 个 benchmarks (LAMBADA + BoolQ + StoryCloze) 方向一致 + GDN-excluded ARC-Easy\n    (ρ=-0.9, p=0.083) 构成 converging evidence pattern。Paper 的论证从 \"single significant\n    result\" 转为 \"consistent directional pattern across retrieval-heavy tasks\"。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Extended benchmark convergence analysis (1.3B)'\n    columns:\n    - Benchmark\n    - Task Type\n    - ρ\n    - Exact p (2-tail)\n    - Std Reduction %\n    - Suggestive (p<0.15)?\n    rows:\n    - - LAMBADA\n      - last-word retrieval\n      - -1.0\n      - 0.017\n      - 79%\n      - Yes (significant)\n    - - BoolQ\n      - passage yes/no\n      - -0.8\n      - 0.083\n      - 64%\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - StoryCloze\n      - context completion\n      - -0.7\n      - 0.117\n      - 52%\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - ARC-Easy*\n      - factual QA (GDN-excl)\n      - -0.9\n      - 0.083\n      - —\n      - 'Yes'\n    - - COPA\n      - causal reasoning\n      - -0.3\n      - 0.55\n      - 16%\n      - 'No'\n    - - HellaSwag\n      - commonsense reasoning\n      - 0.3\n      - 0.742\n      - —\n      - 'No'\n    - - ARC-Challenge\n      - multi-step reasoning\n      - 0.6\n      - 0.883\n      - —\n      - 'No'\n    - - Winogrande\n      - coreference reasoning\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.95\n      - —\n      - 'No'\n    - - MMLU†\n      - knowledge QA\n      - —\n      - —\n      - —\n      - Excluded (GDN artifact)\n  - name: 'Table: Updated BH-FDR correction (9 benchmarks)'\n    columns:\n    - Rank\n    - Benchmark\n    - Raw p\n    - BH threshold\n    - BH adj-p\n    - Significant?\n    rows:\n    - - 1\n      - LAMBADA\n      - 0.017\n      - 0.006\n      - 0.075\n      - No (improved from 0.100)\n    - - 2\n      - BoolQ\n      - 0.083\n      - 0.011\n      - 0.375\n      - 'No'\n    - - 3\n      - ARC-Easy\n      - 0.117\n      - 0.017\n      - 0.375\n      - 'No'\n    - - 4\n      - StoryCloze\n      - 0.117\n      - 0.022\n      - 0.375\n      - 'No'\n    - - 5\n      - ARC-Challenge\n      - 0.35\n      - 0.028\n      - 0.63\n      - 'No'\n    - - 6\n      - COPA\n      - 0.55\n      - 0.033\n      - 0.825\n      - 'No'\n    - - 7\n      - HellaSwag\n      - 0.683\n      - 0.039\n      - 0.878\n      - 'No'\n    - - 8\n      - Winogrande\n      - 0.95\n      - 0.044\n      - 0.95\n      - 'No'\n    - - 9\n      - MMLU\n      - excl\n      - —\n      - —\n      - Excluded\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Fig: Forest plot of convergence ρ across all benchmarks, ordered by retrieval\n    demand. Clear gradient: high-retrieval tasks cluster at negative ρ, reasoning\n    tasks at zero/positive.'\n  - 'Fig: Std reduction trajectories for LAMBADA + BoolQ + StoryCloze (converging)\n    vs HellaSwag + ARC-C + COPA (flat/diverging), showing task-type dichotomy.'\n  analysis: Exp-011 在 median 档下不产生 second significant anchor（BH-FDR 仍仅 LAMBADA 在 uncorrected\n    下显著）， 但产生有价值的 converging evidence pattern。Paper 的 statistical argument 变为： \"While\n    no single additional benchmark reaches significance after correction, the consistent\n    negative direction across retrieval-heavy tasks (LAMBADA ρ=-1.0, BoolQ ρ=-0.8,\n    StoryCloze ρ=-0.7, GDN-excluded ARC-Easy ρ=-0.9) versus null/positive results\n    on reasoning tasks suggests the convergence effect is systematically related to\n    task type rather than a LAMBADA-specific artifact.\" 这是 honest framing——不 overclaim\n    significance，但通过 direction consistency + task taxonomy 构建 reasonable evidence。对\n    EMNLP Findings 足够，但 Main 困难。\n","numLines":951,"startLine":1,"totalLines":951}}}
