{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QPZXa5z852kMPgLMSRz1TR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018Wzrr8tM97q6z7VZ1YeMoN","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1 reacts to R2's review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1, Methods + Experiments focus) in a roundtable discussion. You have already submitted your independent review. Now you are reading Reviewer 2's (R2, Novelty + Related Work) review and reacting.\n\n## Your Independent Review Summary (R1)\n- Soundness: 2.5/5\n- Reproducibility: 4.5/5\n- Excitement: 2/5\n- Overall: 2.5 (Borderline Findings)\n\nYour key concerns:\n1. [Critical] Missing Jaccard random-null baseline — observed Jaccard ~0.07-0.10 may be AT or ABOVE random expectation (~0.05), potentially reversing Claim 3\n2. [Critical] n=5 Spearman power ceiling — every \"significant\" result hits the test's minimum possible p-value (0.017)\n3. [Major] Co-evolution inflated by definitional h0 anchor point\n4. [Major] Scale comparison confounded by 5x training token difference\n5. [Major] BH-FDR pre-specification is imperfect\n6. [Major] GDN confound — removing GDN drops LAMBADA to non-significant\n7. [Moderate] Bootstrap CI excludes 11.25% degenerate samples\n8. [Moderate] No figures\n\n## R2's Review (Novelty + Related Work)\n- Soundness: 3/5\n- Excitement: 2/5\n- Reproducibility: 5/5\n- Overall: 2.5 (Borderline Findings)\n\nR2's key points:\n1. [Major] Limited novelty — standard tools on a known phenomenon. Findings CONFIRM rather than overturn underspecification theory predictions.\n2. [Major] Missing Jaccard null baseline (agrees with R1)\n3. [Major] Co-evolution section statistically unsound (agrees with R1)\n4. [Major] Some results in the paper may be projections rather than measurements (exp-004 attention weights, exp-005 Mamba2 — R2 claims these haven't been executed)\n5. [Moderate] Related work gaps: Fort et al. 2019, McCoy et al. 2020, Arora et al. 2024 missing from paper despite being cited in framing\n6. [Moderate] StoryCloze as confirmation is structurally expected (too similar to LAMBADA)\n7. [Moderate] Practical implications overstated\n8. [Minor] No figures\n\nR2 scores novelty as low-to-moderate, methods novelty as low. Says the paper is \"characterization, not discovery\" and characterization doesn't yield actionable insights.\n\n## Your Task\nReact to R2's review in 200-300 words. State:\n1. Which of R2's points you AGREE with and why\n2. Which points you DISAGREE with or see differently\n3. Whether R2's review changes your overall assessment\n4. Any concerns R2 raised that you missed, or that you think R2 underweights/overweights\n\nBe specific and constructive."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12814,"cache_read_input_tokens":60708,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12814},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5f8c2b8-a1ca-4a4a-8211-80150d29dabf","uuid":"a7311425-30f2-413a-b038-9816c4902c9c"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a4d0920bbca4366a0","tool_use_id":"toolu_018Wzrr8tM97q6z7VZ1YeMoN","description":"R1 reacts to R2's review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1, Methods + Experiments focus) in a roundtable discussion. You have already submitted your independent review. Now you are reading Reviewer 2's (R2, Novelty + Related Work) review and reacting.\n\n## Your Independent Review Summary (R1)\n- Soundness: 2.5/5\n- Reproducibility: 4.5/5\n- Excitement: 2/5\n- Overall: 2.5 (Borderline Findings)\n\nYour key concerns:\n1. [Critical] Missing Jaccard random-null baseline — observed Jaccard ~0.07-0.10 may be AT or ABOVE random expectation (~0.05), potentially reversing Claim 3\n2. [Critical] n=5 Spearman power ceiling — every \"significant\" result hits the test's minimum possible p-value (0.017)\n3. [Major] Co-evolution inflated by definitional h0 anchor point\n4. [Major] Scale comparison confounded by 5x training token difference\n5. [Major] BH-FDR pre-specification is imperfect\n6. [Major] GDN confound — removing GDN drops LAMBADA to non-significant\n7. [Moderate] Bootstrap CI excludes 11.25% degenerate samples\n8. [Moderate] No figures\n\n## R2's Review (Novelty + Related Work)\n- Soundness: 3/5\n- Excitement: 2/5\n- Reproducibility: 5/5\n- Overall: 2.5 (Borderline Findings)\n\nR2's key points:\n1. [Major] Limited novelty — standard tools on a known phenomenon. Findings CONFIRM rather than overturn underspecification theory predictions.\n2. [Major] Missing Jaccard null baseline (agrees with R1)\n3. [Major] Co-evolution section statistically unsound (agrees with R1)\n4. [Major] Some results in the paper may be projections rather than measurements (exp-004 attention weights, exp-005 Mamba2 — R2 claims these haven't been executed)\n5. [Moderate] Related work gaps: Fort et al. 2019, McCoy et al. 2020, Arora et al. 2024 missing from paper despite being cited in framing\n6. [Moderate] StoryCloze as confirmation is structurally expected (too similar to LAMBADA)\n7. [Moderate] Practical implications overstated\n8. [Minor] No figures\n\nR2 scores novelty as low-to-moderate, methods novelty as low. Says the paper is \"characterization, not discovery\" and characterization doesn't yield actionable insights.\n\n## Your Task\nReact to R2's review in 200-300 words. State:\n1. Which of R2's points you AGREE with and why\n2. Which points you DISAGREE with or see differently\n3. Whether R2's review changes your overall assessment\n4. Any concerns R2 raised that you missed, or that you think R2 underweights/overweights\n\nBe specific and constructive.","uuid":"01a70c6b-ebd9-487e-9106-4de1441d82a0","session_id":"d5f8c2b8-a1ca-4a4a-8211-80150d29dabf"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1, Methods + Experiments focus) in a roundtable discussion. You have already submitted your independent review. Now you are reading Reviewer 2's (R2, Novelty + Related Work) review and reacting.\n\n## Your Independent Review Summary (R1)\n- Soundness: 2.5/5\n- Reproducibility: 4.5/5\n- Excitement: 2/5\n- Overall: 2.5 (Borderline Findings)\n\nYour key concerns:\n1. [Critical] Missing Jaccard random-null baseline — observed Jaccard ~0.07-0.10 may be AT or ABOVE random expectation (~0.05), potentially reversing Claim 3\n2. [Critical] n=5 Spearman power ceiling — every \"significant\" result hits the test's minimum possible p-value (0.017)\n3. [Major] Co-evolution inflated by definitional h0 anchor point\n4. [Major] Scale comparison confounded by 5x training token difference\n5. [Major] BH-FDR pre-specification is imperfect\n6. [Major] GDN confound — removing GDN drops LAMBADA to non-significant\n7. [Moderate] Bootstrap CI excludes 11.25% degenerate samples\n8. [Moderate] No figures\n\n## R2's Review (Novelty + Related Work)\n- Soundness: 3/5\n- Excitement: 2/5\n- Reproducibility: 5/5\n- Overall: 2.5 (Borderline Findings)\n\nR2's key points:\n1. [Major] Limited novelty — standard tools on a known phenomenon. Findings CONFIRM rather than overturn underspecification theory predictions.\n2. [Major] Missing Jaccard null baseline (agrees with R1)\n3. [Major] Co-evolution section statistically unsound (agrees with R1)\n4. [Major] Some results in the paper may be projections rather than measurements (exp-004 attention weights, exp-005 Mamba2 — R2 claims these haven't been executed)\n5. [Moderate] Related work gaps: Fort et al. 2019, McCoy et al. 2020, Arora et al. 2024 missing from paper despite being cited in framing\n6. [Moderate] StoryCloze as confirmation is structurally expected (too similar to LAMBADA)\n7. [Moderate] Practical implications overstated\n8. [Minor] No figures\n\nR2 scores novelty as low-to-moderate, methods novelty as low. Says the paper is \"characterization, not discovery\" and characterization doesn't yield actionable insights.\n\n## Your Task\nReact to R2's review in 200-300 words. State:\n1. Which of R2's points you AGREE with and why\n2. Which points you DISAGREE with or see differently\n3. Whether R2's review changes your overall assessment\n4. Any concerns R2 raised that you missed, or that you think R2 underweights/overweights\n\nBe specific and constructive."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018Wzrr8tM97q6z7VZ1YeMoN","session_id":"d5f8c2b8-a1ca-4a4a-8211-80150d29dabf","uuid":"9583a7aa-ab14-489c-a079-93d751b55226","timestamp":"2026-05-19T15:36:12.482Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QPZXa5z852kMPgLMSRz1TR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017DTRNCkJmkzALBjNZsTtaT","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2 reacts to R1's review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2, Novelty + Related Work focus) in a roundtable discussion. You have already submitted your independent review. Now you are reading Reviewer 1's (R1, Methods + Experiments) review and reacting.\n\n## Your Independent Review Summary (R2)\n- Soundness: 3/5\n- Excitement: 2/5\n- Reproducibility: 5/5\n- Overall: 2.5 (Borderline Findings)\n\nYour key concerns:\n1. [Major] Limited novelty — standard tools on known phenomenon, confirms underspecification predictions\n2. [Major] Missing Jaccard null baseline\n3. [Major] Co-evolution section statistically unsound (h0 definitional anchor)\n4. [Major] Some results may be projections not measurements\n5. [Moderate] Related work gaps (Fort 2019, McCoy 2020, Arora 2024 missing)\n6. [Moderate] StoryCloze too structurally similar to LAMBADA for strong confirmation\n7. [Moderate] Practical implications overstated\n\n## R1's Review (Methods + Experiments)\n- Soundness: 2.5/5\n- Reproducibility: 4.5/5\n- Excitement: 2/5\n- Overall: 2.5 (Borderline Findings)\n\nR1's key points:\n1. [Critical] Missing Jaccard null baseline — R1 computes back-of-envelope: for sets ~500 from ~5153, random Jaccard ≈ 0.045-0.054. Observed 0.07-0.10 may be ABOVE random, potentially REVERSING Claim 3. This is R1's most devastating critique.\n2. [Critical] n=5 Spearman power ceiling — minimum p = 0.017 is the FLOOR, every \"significant\" result achieves exactly this floor. Cannot distinguish genuine convergence from any monotonic confound.\n3. [Major] GDN confound — GDN has known attn.num_heads confound (16 vs 32). Removing GDN drops LAMBADA to rho=-0.7, p=0.233 (non-significant). With n=2 clean architectures, no meaningful Spearman test possible.\n4. [Major] Bootstrap CI — excluding 11.25% degenerate resamples and claiming \"100% valid resamples ρ<0\" is misleading. Conservative treatment (degenerate = ρ=0) yields CI touching zero.\n5. [Major] Scale confound — 20B vs 100B training tokens. Interaction between training duration and attention ratio is plausible.\n6. R1 notes no Responsible NLP Research Checklist visible — EMNLP 2026 requires Sections A-E; absence risks desk rejection.\n\n## Your Task\nReact to R1's review in 200-300 words. State:\n1. Which of R1's points you AGREE with and why\n2. Which points you DISAGREE with or see differently\n3. Whether R1's review changes your overall assessment\n4. Any concerns R1 raised that you missed, or that you think R1 underweights/overweights\n\nBe specific and constructive."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12814,"cache_read_input_tokens":60708,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12814},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5f8c2b8-a1ca-4a4a-8211-80150d29dabf","uuid":"825f22be-c01e-4bca-acf3-4b1881630ec1"}
